        {"h2_html": "What Podium <em>does well</em>",
         "body_html": """<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">Podium built its name on customer communication, and it earned it. It is known for review generation, for pulling messages from text, web chat, Google, and Facebook into one inbox, and for letting customers pay by text. More recently it has added an AI layer that responds to and qualifies leads and can book appointments (features and plans as of publication, so check Podium's own site for the current details). Tens of thousands of local businesses use it, and the owners who like it tend to really like how it tidies up the back and forth with customers.</p><p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch;margin-top:1rem">If your website and marketing are already handled and what you want is a strong, focused tool for reviews, two-way messaging, and getting paid, Podium is a serious option, and we will say so plainly. It is a software platform, which means you or someone on your team logs in and runs it day to day. For plenty of owners that is exactly right. It is still worth knowing what a tool is built to do, and what it leaves you to handle yourself, before you sign up, which is the honest point of a page like this one.</p>"""},
